# The step of the sum of an array of two limbs that the program supplies (milestone2.md, "Folds",
# "Arrays that the program fills"): both limbs of the element pass through guard, rule R3, then
# add_2_2. Its claims are those of add_2_2.
kernel:        sum_entry_step_2
input:         s = s0 s1
input:         supplied x = x0 x1
output:        t = t0 t1
value:         s+x
requires:      normalized s
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       normalized t
ensures:       error t R c=3/(1-4*u) k=2 t=0
min_precision: 3
theorem:       proofs/theories/StepKernels.v sum_entry_step_2_correct
source:        add_2_2 on a guarded element (rule R3); JMP17 Alg. 6, bound from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge spec

g0       = guard(x0)
g1       = guard(x1)
(t0, t1) = add_2_2(s0, s1, g0, g1)
